"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,229\nThe Learning Brain. Series 3: Generative AI\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,365\nEpisode 7\n\n3\n00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:09,541\nAutomation bias\n\n4\n00:00:12,341 --> 00:00:15,988\nTwenty seven radiologists read fifty mammograms,\n\n5\n00:00:16,301 --> 00:00:20,823\neach with a rating suggested by what they were told was an AI system.\n\n6\n00:00:21,299 --> 00:00:22,747\nIn twelve of the cases,\n\n7\n00:00:22,993 --> 00:00:25,426\nthe suggestion was deliberately wrong.\n\n8\n00:00:25,596 --> 00:00:27,128\nWhen the AI was right,\n\n9\n00:00:27,365 --> 00:00:31,084\nall three experience groups were about eighty percent accurate.\n\n10\n00:00:31,589 --> 00:00:32,582\nWhen it was wrong,\n\n11\n00:00:32,845 --> 00:00:35,984\ninexperienced readers fell to about twenty percent.\n\n12\n00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:40,098\nModerately experienced readers fell to about twenty five.\n\n13\n00:00:40,631 --> 00:00:44,299\nEven very experienced readers fell to about forty five.\n\n14\n00:00:44,469 --> 00:00:50,281\nThis is automation bias: the pull to accept a machine's answer over your own judgement.\n\n15\n00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:54,687\nIt shows up in two ways: acting on a wrong suggestion,\n\n16\n00:00:54,831 --> 00:00:57,455\nand failing to notice what the system missed.\n\n17\n00:00:57,625 --> 00:00:58,857\nIt is a shortcut.\n\n18\n00:00:59,247 --> 00:01:04,045\nChecking takes effort, and a confident suggestion lowers the felt need to check.\n\n19\n00:01:04,582 --> 00:01:07,937\nExpertise helps, but it does not make anyone immune.\n\n20\n00:01:08,107 --> 00:01:11,743\nAn editorial alongside the study suggested safeguards: training,\n\n21\n00:01:12,089 --> 00:01:16,284\naccountability with regular feedback on performance,\n\n22\n00:01:16,554 --> 00:01:18,894\ntransparent and validated systems,\n\n23\n00:01:19,182 --> 00:01:22,765\nand AI that runs in the background as a second check.\n\n24\n00:01:22,935 --> 00:01:23,733\nA caution.\n\n25\n00:01:24,162 --> 00:01:25,620\nThis was one experiment,\n\n26\n00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:28,917\nwith a purported AI and a small number of readers.\n\n27\n00:01:29,322 --> 00:01:33,135\nBut automation bias itself has been studied for decades,\n\n28\n00:01:33,317 --> 00:01:35,111\nfrom aviation to medicine.\n\n29\n00:01:35,281 --> 00:01:36,033\nFor teaching.\n\n30\n00:01:36,477 --> 00:01:40,267\nHave students commit to their own answer before they see the AI's.\n\n31\n00:01:40,604 --> 00:01:44,192\nSeed some AI suggestions with deliberate errors,\n\n32\n00:01:44,273 --> 00:01:45,866\nand debrief who caught them.\n\n33\n00:01:46,277 --> 00:01:50,931\nAnd give feedback on how often students overrode the AI when they should have.\n\n34\n00:01:51,101 --> 00:01:54,356\nExpertise does not switch off automation bias.\n\n35\n00:01:54,739 --> 00:01:58,230\nPractice at disagreeing is the defence we can teach.\n\n"
